# id: EXPAND-ignores-batch-history
# blinds: a DeleteRange covering earlier writes in its own batch
# covering-lane: cpp-test
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-build
# expect-control: alive
#
# NOT IN THE CATALOGUE. Section 8.1 states the intra-batch rule -- at the
# DeleteRange the expansion covers the current state AND keys written earlier in
# the same batch, and a Set after it re-adds the key -- and the rule has no
# mechanism behind it until something plants its absence.
#
# The defect is invisible to every single-op workload and to every batch whose
# DeleteRange comes first. It appears only when a batch writes a key and then
# deletes a range containing it, which is exactly what snapshot application's
# clear-then-ingest does when the ingest and the clear share a batch.
#
# It is also the half that CANNOT be fixed at replay: the WAL records the
# expansion, so an expansion that missed a key records a log that is faithfully
# replayed into the wrong state forever.
--- a/engine-cpp/src/db.cc	2026-08-25 03:07:35
+++ b/engine-cpp/src/db.cc	2026-08-25 03:07:35
@@ -122,12 +122,7 @@
